From: mscharged-port
Subject: Give the online ranking overlay SHNavigation's inline timer visibility
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native compiler contract; no game behavior change.

OnlineRankingOverlay::UpdateResultsDisplay calls
SHNavigation::SetTimerVisible, whose body is the inline definition in
SHNavigation.inl. OnlineRanking.cpp includes only SHNavigation.h, so the
native compiler emitted an external call that no unit defines (retail
has an out-of-line copy at 0x801CA9E0). The frontend module still links,
as a shared object may leave symbols undefined, and the dynamic loader
resolves it lazily: the first ranked results overlay (0746) ended the
process with "symbol lookup error" and exit status 127.

Natively the unit includes the inline header, as fePopupMenu.cpp does.

diff --git a/src/Game/FE/OnlineRanking.cpp b/src/Game/FE/OnlineRanking.cpp
index 8dbb6a2..d794e1e 100644
--- a/src/Game/FE/OnlineRanking.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/FE/OnlineRanking.cpp
@@ -13,6 +13,10 @@
 #include "Game/NetworkStatsManager.h"
 #include "Game/OverlayManager.h"
 #include "Game/SH/SHNavigation.h"
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+// SetTimerVisible's inline body; no native unit emits it out of line.
+#include "Game/SH/SHNavigation.inl"
+#endif
 #include "Game/SH/SHPausePostGame.h"
 #include "NL/nlBind.h"
 #include "NL/nlFormat.h"
